    (3) Additional standard deduction for aged and blind

    For purposes of paragraph (1), the additional standard deduction is the sum of each additional amount to which the taxpayer is entitled under subsection (f).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0017; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(3); source-lines: 41-43; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope StandardDeduction:
  definition additional_under_c3 equals
    let grants equals
      W.injections_for_3_13 of injections, P.pred_s63_c_3_3, taxpayer.id, W.num_key of taxable_year in
    if W.injected_holds of grants
    then
      (match (W.injected_money of grants, 2) with pattern
       -- Absent: $0
       -- Present content m: m)
    else
      (output of AgedOrBlind with {
         -- world: world -- injections: injections -- taxpayer: taxpayer
         -- taxable_year: taxable_year
         -- married: filing_status.married
         -- surviving_spouse: filing_status.surviving_spouse
         # §151(b) and the age/blindness test must refer to the same spouse.
         -- exempt_spouses: exempt_spouses
         }).additional
```

    (5) Limitation on basic standard deduction in the case of certain dependents

    In the case of an individual with respect to whom a deduction under section 151 is allowable to another taxpayer for a taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the individual's taxable year begins, the basic standard deduction applicable to such individual for such individual's taxable year shall not exceed the greater of-


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0018; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(5); source-lines: 45-47; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
## The condition is shared by the public §63(c)(5) result and the branch that
## decides whether its income-dependent cap must be evaluated.
declaration dependent_cap_applies content boolean
  depends on injections content list of W.Injection,
             taxpayer content W.Entity,
             taxable_year content integer,
             dependent_of_another content boolean
  equals
    dependent_of_another
    or (W.injected_holds of
          (W.injections_for_3_23 of injections, P.pred_s151_b_applies_3,
             taxpayer.id, W.num_key of taxable_year))
    or (W.injected_holds of
          (W.injections_for_3_23 of injections, P.pred_s151_c_applies_3,
             taxpayer.id, W.num_key of taxable_year))
```

```catala
scope DependentCap:
  definition capped equals
    dependent_cap_applies of
      injections, taxpayer, taxable_year, dependent_of_another

scope DependentCap:
  definition cap equals
    Money.max of statutory_floor, earned_income_floor
```

```catala-metadata
declaration scope DependentCap:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## §151(b)/(c) allowable to another taxpayer, derived by §151 now that the
  ## section exists; the cases also inject it directly.
  input dependent_of_another content boolean
  output capped content boolean
  output statutory_floor content money
  output earned_income_floor content money
  output cap content money
```



        (A) $500, or


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0019; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(5)(A); source-lines: 49-49; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope DependentCap:
  definition statutory_floor equals $500
```

        (B) the sum of $250 and such individual's earned income.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0020; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(5)(B); source-lines: 51-51; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope DependentCap:
  definition earned_income_floor equals
    $250 + (output of Inc.GrossIncomeIndividual with {
              -- world: world -- person: taxpayer
              -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).total
```

    (6) Certain individuals, etc., not eligible for standard deduction

    In the case of-


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0021; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6); source-lines: 53-55; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope NotEligible:
  definition not_eligible equals
    subparagraph_a or subparagraph_b or subparagraph_d
```

```catala-metadata
declaration overlaps_year content boolean
  depends on starts content list of date,
             ends content optional of date,
             y content integer
  equals
    ((number of starts) = 0
     or (exists d among starts such that d <= (W.last_day_year of y)))
    and (match ends with pattern
         -- Absent: true
         -- Present content d: (W.first_day_year of y) <= d)

declaration scope NotEligible:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input married content boolean
  input joint_return content boolean
  ## Every §7703 spouse, not the first: the Prolog backtracks over
  ## `s7703(Taxp,Spouse,_,Taxy)` and any of them may be the one who itemizes.
  ## See D71.
  input spouses content list of W.Entity
  output subparagraph_a content boolean
  output subparagraph_b content boolean
  output subparagraph_d content boolean
  output not_eligible content boolean
```



        (A) a married individual filing a separate return where either spouse itemizes deductions,


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0022; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6)(A); source-lines: 57-57; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope NotEligible:
  definition subparagraph_a equals
    married and not joint_return
    and (exists ev among (W.deduction_event_values of world) such that
           (ev.agents contains taxpayer
                or (exists sp among spouses such that ev.agents contains sp))
           and (match ev.evidence with pattern
                -- Undated: false
                -- DatedClaim content d:
                     (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= d
                     and d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)
                -- DatedAmount content occurrence:
                     (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= occurrence.start
                     and occurrence.start <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)))
```

        (B) a nonresident alien individual, or


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0023; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6)(B); source-lines: 59-59; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope NotEligible:
  definition subparagraph_b equals
    exists ev among (W.nonresident_alien_event_values of world) such that
      ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and overlaps_year of ev.starts, ev.ends, taxable_year
```

        (D) an estate or trust, common trust fund, or partnership,


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0024; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6)(D); source-lines: 61-61; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope NotEligible:
  definition subparagraph_d equals
    exists ev among (W.business_trust_event_values of world) such that
      ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and overlaps_year of ev.starts, ev.ends, taxable_year
```

    the standard deduction shall be zero.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0025; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(6):flush; source-lines: 63-63; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
