    (7) Special rules for taxable years 2018 through 2025

    In the case of a taxable year beginning after December 31, 2017, and before January 1, 2026-

    Paragraph (2) shall be applied-


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0026; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(7); source-lines: 65-69; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala-metadata
declaration in_2018_2025 content boolean
  depends on y content integer
  equals y > 2017 and y < 2026
```

        (i) by substituting "$18,000" for "$4,400" in subparagraph (B), and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0027; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(7)(i); source-lines: 71-71; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration head_of_household_basic content money
  depends on y content integer
  equals if in_2018_2025 of y then $18,000 else $4,400
```

        (ii) by substituting "$12,000" for "$3,000" in subparagraph (C).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0028; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(c)(7)(ii); source-lines: 73-73; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration residual_basic content money
  depends on y content integer
  equals if in_2018_2025 of y then $12,000 else $3,000
```

(d) Itemized deductions

For purposes of this subtitle, the term "itemized deductions" means the deductions allowable under this chapter other than-


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0029; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(d); source-lines: 75-77; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope ItemizedDeductions:
  definition total equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each ev among
        (list of e among (W.deduction_event_values of world)
         such that e.agents contains taxpayer)
       to (match ev.evidence with pattern
           -- Undated: $0
           -- DatedClaim content d: $0
           -- DatedAmount content occurrence:
                (if (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= occurrence.start
                    and occurrence.start <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)
                 then occurrence.amount
                 else $0)
          # `agent_/2` is a relation like the other two: stating it twice gives
          # the `findall` two solutions and counts the deduction twice. Same
          # reading as D40, one section over. See D56.
          * (decimal of (Inc.role_count of ev.agents, taxpayer))))

  # `length(Amounts,L), L>0` counts the `findall`'s solutions, and every goal
  # in it has to succeed for there to be one -- `amount_(Deduction,Amount)`
  # included. A deduction event with a date but no amount is not a solution, so
  # the taxpayer does not itemize and §63(b) takes over. See D72.

scope ItemizedDeductions:
  definition itemizes equals
    itemizes_from_world of world, taxpayer, taxable_year
```

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ItemizedDeductions:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  output itemizes content boolean
  output total content money

declaration itemizes_from_world content boolean
  depends on world content W.World,
             taxpayer content W.Entity,
             taxable_year content integer
  equals
    exists ev among (W.deduction_event_values of world) such that
      ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and (match ev.evidence with pattern
           -- Undated: false
           -- DatedClaim content d: false
           -- DatedAmount content occurrence:
                (W.first_day_year of taxable_year) <= occurrence.start
                and occurrence.start <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
```



    (1) the deductions allowable in arriving at adjusted gross income, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0030; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(d)(1); source-lines: 79-79; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
