(f) Aged or blind additional amounts

    (1) Additional amounts for the aged

    The taxpayer shall be entitled to an additional amount of $600-


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0032; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(1); source-lines: 85-87; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope AgedOrBlind:
  definition counts equals
    (if aged_self then 1 else 0)
    + (if aged_spouse then 1 else 0)
    + (if blind_self then 1 else 0)
    # DEVIATIONS.md D6: the gold uses 600 here where every sibling uses 1.
    + (if blind_spouse then 600 else 0)

scope AgedOrBlind:
  definition additional equals
    (per_entitlement of married, surviving_spouse) * (decimal of counts)
```

```catala-metadata
declaration attained_65 content boolean
  depends on birth content date, y content integer
  equals
    ((W.last_day_year of y) - birth)
      >= ((W.last_day_year of (y + 65)) - (W.last_day_year of y))

declaration scope AgedOrBlind:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  input married content boolean
  input surviving_spouse content boolean
  ## The §7703 spouses for whom §151(b) allows the additional exemption --- a
  ## *list*, because `s63_f_1_B(Taxp,Spouse,Taxy)` carries one `Spouse` through
  ## both halves of the clause: the same person has to be over 65 *and* be the
  ## one §151(b) allows. Reading the two halves off different spouses gave a
  ## couple filing jointly a $600 entitlement SARA never grants; see D80. The
  ## cases inject this, and D2 records that the Prolog's arity-2 guard is
  ## vacuous.
  input exempt_spouses content list of W.Entity
  output aged_self content boolean
  output aged_spouse content boolean
  output blind_self content boolean
  output blind_spouse content boolean
  output counts content integer
  output additional content money
```



        (A) for himself if he has attained age 65 before the close of his taxable year, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0033; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(1)(A); source-lines: 89-89; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope AgedOrBlind:
  definition aged_self equals
    (W.injected_holds of (W.injections_for_2_12 of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_A_2, taxpayer.id, W.num_key of taxable_year))
    or
    ((not (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_A_2))
     and (exists ev among (W.birth_event_values of world) such that
            ev.agents contains taxpayer
            and (match ev.starts with pattern
                 -- Absent: false
                 -- Present content d: attained_65 of d, taxable_year)))
```

        (B) for the spouse of the taxpayer if the spouse has attained age 65 before the close of the taxable year and an additional exemption is allowable to the taxpayer for such spouse under section 151(b).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0034; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(1)(B); source-lines: 91-91; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope AgedOrBlind:
  definition aged_spouse equals
    (W.injected_holds of (W.injections_for_3_13 of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_B_3, taxpayer.id, W.num_key of taxable_year))
    or
    ((not (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s63_f_1_B_3))
     and married
     and (exists sp among exempt_spouses such that
            exists ev among (W.birth_event_values of world) such that
              ev.agents contains sp
              and (match ev.starts with pattern
                   -- Absent: false
                   -- Present content d: attained_65 of d, taxable_year)))
```

    (2) Additional amount for blind

    The taxpayer shall be entitled to an additional amount of $600-


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0035; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(2); source-lines: 93-95; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
# This structural heading introduces no rule independently of its immediately following subprovisions.
```

        (A) for himself if he is blind at the close of the taxable year, and


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0036; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(2)(A); source-lines: 97-97; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope AgedOrBlind:
  definition blind_self equals
    exists ev among (W.blindness_event_values of world) such that
      ev.agents contains taxpayer
      and (match ev.starts with pattern
           -- Absent: false
           -- Present content d: d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
```

        (B) for the spouse of the taxpayer if the spouse is blind as of the close of the taxable year and an additional exemption is allowable to the taxpayer for such spouse under section 151(b).


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0037; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(2)(B); source-lines: 99-99; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
scope AgedOrBlind:
  definition blind_spouse equals
    married
    and (exists sp among exempt_spouses such that
           exists ev among (W.blindness_event_values of world) such that
             ev.agents contains sp
             and (match ev.starts with pattern
                  -- Absent: false
                  -- Present content d: d <= (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)))
```

    For purposes of subparagraph (B), if the spouse dies during the taxable year the determination of whether such spouse is blind shall be made as of the time of such death.


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0038; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(2):flush; source-lines: 101-101; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
# This is continuation prose; its legal effect is implemented in the preceding provision block.
```

    (3) Higher amount for certain unmarried individuals

    In the case of an individual who is not married and is not a surviving spouse, paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be applied by substituting "$750" for "$600".


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section63:b0039; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section63(f)(3); source-lines: 103-105; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration per_entitlement content money
  depends on married content boolean, surviving_spouse content boolean
  equals if (not married) and (not surviving_spouse) then $750 else $600
```

